{
  "about": "Modern IAF's sound table: one row per sound code (and sub code) the flight scene plays (docs/sound.md §3-§5), each naming its clip in this folder (sources: SOURCES.md). Every clip is 22050 Hz mono Ogg Vorbis. Compiled by iaf-sim own into assets/converted/own/resource/soundfiles/soundprop.trx (the columns of docs/sound.md §1). category: engine / effect / speech (the Preferences volume that applies); play: loop / once; 3d: placed at the object, heard from min_m to max_m; volume_in / volume_out: in the cockpit / outside; channel: a logical channel (0 none). Our values (inferred): the engine 0.6 inside the cockpit, the lever sounds 0.75; explosions heard to 3 km. by_name: the clips the shared code opens by file name (g_effects.gd cock_g_02.wav, the G strain; terrain_view.gd EndWorld.wav, the map edge; radio.gd KCH2.WAV, the radio click, and key_on.ogg / key_off.ogg, the keyed quiet around a radio call; sim_flight.gd radio_gap.ogg, the 0.6 s between the player's call and the tower's answer; each the .ogg of that name, sound_table.gd falls back from .wav to .ogg); g_effects.gd's cock_bty_over.wav is left out on purpose (the VMS has no Over-G voice).",
  "by_name": ["cock_g_02.ogg", "endworld.ogg", "kch2.ogg", "key_on.ogg", "key_off.ogg", "radio_gap.ogg"],
  "rows": [
